; Auto-wah: a filter that opens and closes on its own. On FM the modulator's
; TL is the filter, so a sin on it sweeps the brightness; on a note-length
; clock the wah locks to the tempo. It is an inline sweep on the track, not a
; macro: a macro starts over with every note, a sweep runs across them. :dr3 0
; stops the voice's own pluck on that operator, so the wah is the only filter.
; An eighth-note wah, then a slow one over the bar.
(import "presets/waveforms/set.mmlisp")

(def line :len 16 c c > c < c  e- c c > c <  c b- c g  f e- c c)

(fm1 :tempo 112 :oct 2 acid-saw :dr3 0
  :tl3 (sin 12..56 :len 8)  (x 2 line)
  :tl3 (sin 12..56 :len 1)  (x 2 line))
